{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And their meal-offering and their libations for the bulls.</b> The bulls of the festival are seventy, corresponding to the seventy nations, and they diminish and go on decreasing — a sign of their destruction. And in the days of the Temple they shielded them from afflictions (Sukkah 55)." "<b>And for the lambs.</b> Corresponding to Israel, who are called ״שֵׂה פְזוּרָה״ (Jeremiah 50). And they are fixed, and their number is ninety-eight — to eliminate from them the ninety-eight curses in Mishneh Torah. On the second day it says וְנִסְכֵּיהֶם, and He did not change the expression except for derash, as our Rabbis, of blessed memory, said (Sifrei; Shabbat 150): on the second — וְנִסְכֵּיהֶם; on the sixth — וּנְסָכֶיהָ; on the seventh — כְּמִשְׁפָּטָם. Mem, yod, mem — behold, here is מַיִם — an allusion to the water-libation on the festival from the Torah."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:13:15.484471964Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}